course: dictionary
lesson: 4812
title: Noun or verb? Hunch in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hunch is a word with two jobs. As a noun, it is a feeling that something is true, even though you have no proof. «I had a hunch the missing sock was behind the sofa.» You cannot touch a hunch, so the sentence tells you it is a feeling.
explain: As a verb, hunch means to bend your back and shoulders forward and up. «She hunched over her desk all afternoon.» Picture her head down and her back curved. People often hunch when they are cold, tired or worried: «He hunched against the cold wind.»
explain: Use the clues around the word to decide. If the sentence is about a guess or a feeling, hunch is a noun. If it is about how someone sits, stands or holds their body, hunch is a verb. Check by swapping in another word: "guess" fits the noun, and "bend over" fits the verb.
fact: A hunch is a feeling that something is true, with no proof yet.
fact: «Hunched» means bent forward, with the shoulders up and the back curved.
fact: In science, a hunch must be tested with an experiment before people accept it.
fact: Old meaning: a hunch can also be a hump or a lump.
exercise: «I had a hunch the test would be easy, so I read less.» What does hunch mean here? | A loud noise in the hall | A bent back from sitting too long | A heavy bag full of books | *A feeling that something is true, with no proof
exercise: What does hunched mean in «hunched over his desk»? | Standing tall and proud | Lying flat on the floor | *Bent forward, with shoulders up | Jumping up and down
exercise: A scientist says, «My hunch needs testing.» Why? | *Because a hunch is only a feeling, so an experiment must check it | Because a hunch is always right | Because a hunch is a kind of animal | Because a hunch is a type of food
test: «Mole hunched himself up in a hollow tree.» Is Mole standing straight or curled up? | Swimming in a river | Standing straight and tall | *Curled up, bent forward | Flying above the trees
test: Ben says, «I have a hunch my bike is in the shed.» What kind of word is hunch here? | A type of food | A colour | A verb, an action of bending | *A noun, a feeling you have
exam: Which sentence uses hunch as a verb? | Follow your hunch and trust yourself | I had a hunch it would rain | *She hunched her shoulders against the wind | A hunch is a feeling you cannot prove
